title: Heliopolis (ancient Egypt)
description: Ancient Egyptian city located in present-day Ayn Shams, Cairo
key-facts:
  - name: Where it was
    value: Within the Ain Shams and El Matareya districts of northeastern Cairo
    from: Its site is within the boundaries of [[ Ain Shams ]] and [[ El Matareya
      | el-matareya-cairo ]] districts (//kism//) in northeastern [[ Cairo ]].
  - name: What it was
    value: Capital of the Heliopolite or 13th nome of Lower Egypt, and a major
      religious centre
    from: It was the capital of the Heliopolite or 13th [[ Nome |
      nome-egypt#lower-egypt ]] (province or district) of [[ Lower Egypt ]]
      and a major religious centre.
  - name: How old
    value: One of the oldest cities of ancient Egypt, occupied since prehistoric
      Egypt
    from: One of the oldest cities of ancient Egypt, occupied since [[ prehistoric
      Egypt ]],[[ ^1 ]] it greatly expanded under the [[ Old |
      old-kingdom-of-egypt ]] and [[ Middle Kingdoms | middle-kingdom-of-egypt
      ]].
  - name: The name
    value: Latinised from the Greek Hēlioúpolis, "City of the Sun"
    from: Heliopolis is the [[ Latinised | latinisation-of-names ]] form of the [[
      Greek | ancient-greek-language ]] name //Hēlioúpolis// (Ἡλιούπολις),
      meaning "City of the Sun".
  - name: The obelisk
    value: 21 m (69 ft) of red granite weighing 120 tons (240,000 lbs), believed
      to be the oldest surviving obelisk in the world
    from: The 21 m (69 ft) high red granite obelisk weighs 120 tons (240,000 lbs)
      and is believed to be the oldest surviving obelisk in the world.[[ ^3 ]]
  - name: How deep it lies now
    value: About 15–20 meters (49–66 ft) below the streets of northern Cairo
    from: The ancient city is currently located about 15–20 meters (49–66 ft)
      below the streets of the middle- and lower-class suburbs of [[
      Al-Matariyyah | el-matareya-cairo ]],[[ ^1 ]] [[ Ain Shams ]], and Tel
      Al-Hisn[[ ^21 ]] in northern [[ Cairo ]].
